# The kitty keyboard protocol's flag 8, report all keys as escape codes,
# pushed without flag 1. Flag 8 disambiguates every key by itself, so
# Escape, Alt+A, Up and F1 take their flag 1 forms. A key that makes
# text sends an escape code and no text: Space, Shift+A, Shift+1, A with
# Caps Lock, é and Cyrillic es. Shift+A and Shift+1 carry the unshifted
# key's code. The keypad's 1 and Enter are sent with their own numbers,
# and Shift+Enter is CSI 13 ; 2 u. Each modifier key pressed alone is
# reported with its own number and with its own bit set. A pop puts 0
# in force, and A sends its text again.
# spec: kitty's Comprehensive keyboard handling in terminals: Report all keys as escape codes, Key codes, Modifiers, Functional key definitions; ADR-1005 D13 slice 3
# covers: input.kitty-keyboard
size 20 2
needs key-forms
send "\e[>8u"
key Escape
key a mods=alt
key Up
key F1
key space
key space mods=ctrl
key A mods=shift
cmd key;sym=21;ascii=21;unicode=21;unshifted=31;base=31;mods=1
key A mods=lock
key eacute
key Cyrillic_es
key KP_1 mods=num char="1"
key KP_Enter
key Return mods=shift
key Shift_R mods=shift
key Control_L mods=ctrl
key Alt_L mods=alt
key Super_R mods=logo
key 0xffed mods=hyper
key Meta_L mods=meta
key Num_Lock mods=num
key 0xfe03
key 0xfe11
send "\e[<u"
key A mods=shift
